@topic error.dfa-alphabet
title: DFA-ALPHABET: a symbol outside the recognizer's alphabet
summary: A symbol, a range or a class names a value outside the alphabet the recognizer reads (or the alphabet is unknown).
index: errors
alias: outside the alphabet; unknown alphabet
keywords: dfa, alphabet, bytes, ascii, unicode, surrogate, range
related: concept.recognizers error.dfa-byte-character
docs: DFA-COROUTINE-MILESTONE-2.md
code: CORE SEMANTIC DFA-ALPHABET

== MEANING
bytes are 0..255, ascii 0..127, unicode the Unicode scalar values (a range
that spans the surrogates U+D800..U+DFFF means its scalar values; one wholly
inside them names none). A value outside the alphabet is rejected at run
time by every recognizer: writing one is a mistake.

@example reject
import std::dfa

dfa d over ascii:
    start:
        200 -> accept

0
@caption 200 is no ASCII code
@error CORE SEMANTIC DFA-ALPHABET
@at 5:9
@end

