@topic error.dfa-no-accept
title: DFA-NO-ACCEPT: a state from which nothing is ever accepted
summary: Every path from a reachable state ends in a rejection (from the start: the recognizer accepts no input at all); it is reported where the paths end, not at every state that leads there.
index: errors
alias: never accepts
keywords: dfa, accept, state, closing quote
related: concept.recognizers
docs: DFA-COROUTINE-MILESTONE-2.md
code: CORE SEMANTIC DFA-NO-ACCEPT

== MEANING
A forgotten `accept` -- the closing quote of a string, the last digit of a
fixed-length escape -- leaves a state from which the recognizer can only
reject: it is equivalent to omitting the state.

@example reject
import std::dfa

dfa quoted over ascii:
    start:
        '"' -> body
    body:
        'a'..'z' -> body

0
@caption The closing quote is missing
@error CORE SEMANTIC DFA-NO-ACCEPT
@at 6:5
@end

