@topic error.dfa-unread-beyond-input
title: DFA-UNREAD-BEYOND-INPUT: `accept before N` hands back too many symbols
summary: A recognizer never hands back a symbol it was not given, and a token keeps at least one symbol, so in a state reached after K symbols `accept before N` needs N at most K (at the end, below K).
index: errors
alias: unread count too large; accept before too many; lookahead beyond the token
keywords: dfa, accept before, lookahead, unread, bound, empty token, buffer
related: concept.recognizers error.dfa-call-lookahead
docs: DFA-COROUTINE-MILESTONE-2.md
code: CORE SEMANTIC DFA-UNREAD-BEYOND-INPUT

== MEANING
`accept before N` completes leaving the last N symbols the recognizer was
handed unread: the driver hands them to the next token. They must be the
recognizer's own: the compiler counts the fewest symbols any path to the
state consumes (a call: its callee's shortest token) and checks N against
it. The end of the input is never counted. This is what makes every
recognizer's largest unread count a static bound, and what keeps a driver
that hands the unread symbols to the next token from looping on an empty
one.

== WHAT TO DO
Leave fewer symbols unread, or move the transition to a state that is
reached only after the symbols it hands back.

@example reject
import std::dfa

dfa word over ascii:
    start:
        'a'..'z' -> body
    body:
        'a'..'z' -> body
        ':' -> accept before 2
        end -> accept

0
@caption body may be reached after one symbol: there is only one to hand back with the ':'
@error CORE SEMANTIC DFA-UNREAD-BEYOND-INPUT
@at 8:16
@end

@topic error.dfa-call-lookahead
title: DFA-CALL-LOOKAHEAD: a call continues after a callee that leaves too much
summary: `call DFA then STATE` can reconsider only the symbol the callee completed on, so a callee that leaves more unread is called with `then accept`, which passes its unread symbols on.
index: errors
alias: call lookahead
keywords: dfa, call, delegation, lookahead, accept before, unread
related: concept.recognizers error.dfa-unread-beyond-input
docs: DFA-COROUTINE-MILESTONE-2.md
code: CORE SEMANTIC DFA-CALL-LOOKAHEAD

== MEANING
A recognizer keeps no input: what it reads is handed to it one symbol at
a time and taken. When a callee completes leaving the symbol it completes
on unread, the caller still has that symbol and reconsiders it in STATE;
an earlier one it no longer has. So a callee with `accept before 2` (or
`end -> accept before 1`) can only end its caller's token too: `then
accept` completes the caller with the callee's unread count.

@example reject
import std::dfa

dfa key over ascii:
    start:
        'a'..'z' -> body
    body:
        'a'..'z' -> body
        ':' -> colon
    colon:
        'a'..'z' -> body
        ' ' -> accept before 2
        end -> accept before 1

dfa entry over ascii:
    start:
        'a'..'z' -> call key then rest
    rest:
        ' ' -> accept
        end -> accept

0
@caption key can leave ": " unread, but entry holds only the space
@error CORE SEMANTIC DFA-CALL-LOOKAHEAD
@at 16:26
@end
